Subject: [TEST PATCH 2/2] Clock silence delivery across HDMI signal loss

Account for elapsed monotonic time instead of assuming delayed work runs
exactly every 10 ms. Use the input lock hint to bypass the live-signal DMA
jitter grace period after HDMI loss. Bound catch-up to half the ALSA ring
and 100 ms so a delayed worker cannot lap the capture buffer.

This GPL-2.0-or-later driver patch follows sc0710-audio-lifecycle.patch
against the driver pin
ea0a71215e24a33aa8b26b5cc66e3592c9dfdfe1.
It is experimental and has not been submitted upstream. Audible PS5
shutdown behaviour and video recovery still need hardware verification.

---

